# STILL PHOTO · the frame · the captured plane

a register-emergent of the HRM universe (HERMENEUS, the interpreter) — emergence: natural. moniker ⟦STILL PHOTO:HRM:c57542⟧

**who —** STILL PHOTO — the 2D register: a message rendered as an image, a plane of pixels.
**what —** The spatial register: text→image is free (the console paints your words to a canvas you can download), but image→text is not — reading a picture back into words needs OCR, a model.
**where —** On the screen, on paper, in any captured plane of light.
**why —** Because a picture holds a message a human reads instantly and a machine cannot, without a vision model — the clearest asymmetric boundary.
**how —** By rendering glyphs to a pixel grid (free, deterministic) one way, and by optical character recognition (a model) the other.

**the seal —** Painting the word as a picture is free; reading the picture back is where you must hire a model.

